SUBJECT MATTER EXPERT REVIEW COMMENTS
Project: FAQ Knowledge Base Consolidation
Review Cycle: 2
Date: 2025-03-28

REVIEWER: Marcus Chen — API Platform Architect

Comment on "API Rate Limiting" FAQ:
The rate limit FAQ is accurate but could benefit from explaining the difference between hard and soft limits. Our implementation uses a token bucket algorithm with soft limits (burstable above the stated rate for short periods) and hard limits (absolute ceiling at 2x the stated rate). Including this context would help power users understand why they sometimes see bursts succeed above the stated limit.

Comment on "Webhook Setup" FAQ:
The webhook FAQ should mention that we validate webhook URLs with an initial challenge-response handshake. If the endpoint doesn't respond to the challenge within 5 seconds, the webhook is not created. This is a common source of confusion — users think the webhook config is broken when actually their endpoint isn't responding to the challenge.

Comment on "Database Sharding" FAQ (from Architecture Decision Records):
This ADR content should NOT be included in the public FAQ. The details of our database sharding strategy (consistent hashing ring, 256 virtual nodes) reveals internal architecture that could be used for targeted attacks. The public FAQ should only state that "data is distributed across multiple database servers for scalability" without implementation specifics.

REVIEWER: Lisa Tanaka — Security Engineer

Comment on "SSL Certificate" FAQ:
The SSL FAQ mentions supported cipher suites. While transparency is good, we should avoid enumerating specific cipher suites in public docs — this information helps attackers narrow their attack surface. Recommend replacing with: "The platform supports modern, secure TLS configurations. Insecure protocols and ciphers are automatically rejected." Provide the full cipher list only in enterprise security whitepapers under NDA.
